    "title": "The Lord Lyon's Case for the Baronage",
    "subtitle": "A reader's guide to Innes of Learney's 1945 paper, The Robes of the Feudal Baronage of Scotland",
    "description": "In 1945 the Lord Lyon, Sir Thomas Innes of Learney, set out the evidence that Scotland's minor barons are a titled nobility with their own robes, chapeau and style. A guide to the paper, with page references and sources.",
    "category": "Heritage & Sources",
